# BuildKit reads THIS file (named after the Dockerfile it sits next to) instead
# of a root `.dockerignore`, which the monorepo does not otherwise have.
#
# Root cause of the M10 item-0 build failure: this Dockerfile's build stage
# COPYs source directories (`packages/config`, `packages/edg`, ..., `apps/render`)
# on top of the `node_modules` that `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --filter
# @montaj/render...` had just linked correctly inside the image. On a host
# where `pnpm` creates absolute symlinks into the *host* pnpm store (as it does
# on Windows, e.g. `packages/config/node_modules/typescript ->
# C:\...\node_modules\.pnpm\typescript@5.9.3\node_modules\typescript`), those
# host-relative-looking-but-actually-absolute symlinks got copied straight into
# the image, replacing the container's own valid relative symlinks. Inside the
# container the host path does not exist, so `tsc` (and anything else resolved
# through a workspace package's `node_modules`) fails with MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
#
# `apps/worker-media/Dockerfile.dockerignore` already carries this exact fix;
# this file mirrors it for `apps/render`, whose Dockerfile has the same
# "copy source over an already-installed `node_modules`" shape.

**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/.next*
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/__pycache__
**/.env
**/.env.*
opensource-clipping-main/
postiz-app-main/
scratch/
